diff --git a/docs/obs_grid.md b/docs/obs_grid.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..a3491b0
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/obs_grid.md
@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@
+# OBS window grid capture (`capture = obs`)
+
+Streams up to 10 windows at the same time to a normal Moonlight client. OBS takes the windows, the
+`obs-moonlight-grid` plugin arranges them in a grid on a canvas that has the size of the Moonlight
+stream, and Sunshine encodes that canvas (hardware encoder, no CPU copy) as one video.
+A tap or click on a window of the grid is sent to the real window on the PC.
+
+## Setup
+1. Install the plugin DLL in OBS (`obs-plugins/64bit/obs-moonlight-grid.dll`). Start OBS.
+2. OBS creates a scene named **Moonlight**. Add *Window Capture* sources to it (up to 10).
+   The eye icon switches a window on or off, the order of the list is the order of the grid.
+3. `sunshine.conf`: `capture = obs`
+4. Start a stream from Moonlight (any app entry, e.g. Desktop).
+
+If OBS is not running Sunshine writes a warning to its log and streams the normal capture.
+
+## Notes
+* OBS and Sunshine must use the same GPU. OBS must use the Direct3D 11 renderer.
+* Set OBS to 60 FPS (Settings > Video) for a smooth 60 FPS stream.
+* HDR is not supported in this mode.
+* A click raises the window under the finger, so keyboard input goes to it.
+* Minimised or off-screen windows are restored when touched.
+* Windows run as administrator can only be controlled if Sunshine runs as administrator too.
